{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0528f388", "timestamp": "2026-10-13T16:12:00", "text": "Thanks for sharing, Bob! The structured error logging in Django seems really useful. It could definitely help us with more consistent error reporting. I think adopting a middleware approach could be beneficial for our GraphQL API too. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261013-2-64806"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261013-2-64806"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_1f17ef52", "timestamp": "2026-10-13T16:16:00", "text": "I agree with Bob Taylor. Middleware could be a clean way to handle errors across the board. Plus, structured logging is always a win for debugging. Let's keep this in mind as we move forward.", "utterranceID": "20261013-3-90b31"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261013-3-90b31"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e0273792", "timestamp": "2026-10-13T16:19:00", "text": "Great points! Next, let's look at Kubernetes' Structured Event Logging for Pods. This PR implements structured logging for pod events to facilitate better tracking and analysis. Here's the link: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/3794. Thoughts, Charlie?", "utterranceID": "20261013-4-1e915"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261013-4-1e915"}

