{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_036b54bf", "timestamp": "2026-09-08T04:39:00", "text": "I'll review recent UI updates to see if anything might have caused the spinner issue. Thanks for the teamwork, everyone! 💪", "utterranceID": "20260908-10-5b523"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260908-10-5b523"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T15:16:00", "text": "Hi team, I found some interesting bugs in open-source projects that might help us with our current issues. Let's take a look! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260911-0-4fdf1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260911-0-4fdf1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T15:21:00", "text": "First, there's a 'Keyword Misinterpretation in Query Parsing' issue in Elasticsearch. It seems similar to our keyword misinterpretation problem. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/242. @eid_e01a396c, what do you think?", "utterranceID": "20260911-1-ec082"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260911-1-ec082"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T15:26:00", "text": "Thanks, George! This looks quite similar to what we're facing with CUST-0096. I'll review their parsing logic changes and see if we can apply any insights to our AI model. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260911-2-c4e78"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260911-2-c4e78"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T15:29:00", "text": "Great, Hannah! Next up, we have a 'Suboptimal Query Execution Plan' issue in PostgreSQL. It's about inefficient execution plans causing high resource usage, similar to our query optimization issue. Check it out here: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/243. Charlie, any thoughts?", "utterranceID": "20260911-3-057d6"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260911-3-057d6"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_de315467", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T15:34:00", "text": "This is spot on, George! I'll dive into their approach to optimizing execution plans. It might give us some ideas for improving our database management for CUST-0115. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260911-4-fe4f9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260911-4-fe4f9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-09-11T15:36:00", "text": "Awesome, Charlie! Lastly, there's a 'Persistent Loading Spinner in Component' issue in React. It sounds a lot like our infinite loading spinner problem. Here's the PR: https://github.com/facebook/react/pull/244. Ian, could you take a look?", "utterranceID": "20260911-5-0f15d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260911-5-0f15d"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:25:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Connection Pool Saturation' has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SearchFlow/pull/57.", "utterranceID": "20261024-0-40294"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-0-40294"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:30:00", "text": "To recap, the issue was that our database connection pool was frequently exhausted, causing delays in processing search requests as new connections were queued.", "utterranceID": "20261024-1-f404e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-1-f404e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:31:00", "text": "The root cause was that the connection pool size was insufficient to handle peak loads, leading to connection timeouts and increased latency.", "utterranceID": "20261024-2-74085"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-2-74085"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:36:00", "text": "To resolve this, I increased the connection pool size and implemented a dynamic scaling mechanism that adjusts the pool size based on current load. This should prevent future saturation during peak times.", "utterranceID": "20261024-3-b7bea"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-3-b7bea"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:38:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_a4fa6150! This should really help with the performance issues we've been seeing.", "utterranceID": "20261024-4-156f4"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-4-156f4"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:42:00", "text": "Thanks, Hannah Smith! I'll monitor the performance metrics over the next few days to ensure everything is running smoothly.", "utterranceID": "20261024-5-7f5f4"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-5-7f5f4"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:46:00", "text": "Thanks, @eid_3bcf2a20. Let me know if you notice any anomalies. I'm here to help!", "utterranceID": "20261024-6-e131a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-6-e131a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T12:51:00", "text": "Thanks, everyone! Let's keep an eye on this and regroup if needed. Great teamwork!", "utterranceID": "20261024-7-ece78"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-7-ece78"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:18:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about incorrect cache invalidation causing outdated search results has been resolved. 🎉", "utterranceID": "20261027-0-5454e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-0-5454e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:22:00", "text": "The issue was that the cache invalidation mechanism wasn't triggering correctly when new messages were added. This led to users seeing stale data instead of the most recent messages.", "utterranceID": "20261027-1-e4678"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-1-e4678"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:26:00", "text": "I've fixed it by updating the cache invalidation logic to ensure it triggers every time a new message is added. This involved modifying the event listener to correctly capture and process new message events.", "utterranceID": "20261027-2-eaaa2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-2-eaaa2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:29:00", "text": "You can check the details and review the changes in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SearchFlow/pull/58", "utterranceID": "20261027-3-653ac"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-3-653ac"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:32:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_a4fa6150! Thanks for jumping on this so quickly. I'll test it out and confirm everything is working as expected.", "utterranceID": "20261027-4-d28d3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-4-d28d3"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:35:00", "text": "Thanks, Hannah Smith! This should improve the user experience significantly. Let me know if you need any help with further testing.", "utterranceID": "20261027-5-6e96f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-5-6e96f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_a4fa6150", "timestamp": "2026-10-27T17:39:00", "text": "Thanks, @eid_e01a396c and George. Let me know if you encounter any issues during testing. 😊", "utterranceID": "20261027-6-46f1b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-6-46f1b"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T05:00:00", "text": "To fix this, I modified the event listener to re-enable the input field as soon as the search execution starts, allowing users to modify or cancel the query if needed. This ensures the field is only locked when absolutely necessary.", "utterranceID": "20260819-2-deae5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-2-deae5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_036b54bf", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T05:01:00", "text": "Great work, @eid_e01a396c! This will definitely improve the user experience.", "utterranceID": "20260819-3-df06d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-3-df06d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T05:04:00", "text": "Thanks, Hannah! I was just about to look into this. Glad you got it sorted out.", "utterranceID": "20260819-4-3d3cc"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-4-3d3cc"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T05:07:00", "text": "No problem, George! Let me know if you notice any other issues.", "utterranceID": "20260819-5-4b7c7"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-5-4b7c7"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_036b54bf", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T05:08:00", "text": "I'll test it out today and let you know if anything comes up. Thanks again, Hannah!", "utterranceID": "20260819-6-97a22"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-6-97a22"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-08-22T10:34:00", "text": "Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with SearchFlow that need our immediate attention. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260822-0-eb2a0"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260822-0-eb2a0"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3bcf2a20", "timestamp": "2026-08-22T10:35:00", "text": "First up, we have an issue titled 'Improper Input Sanitization in Search Queries'. The SearchFlow API isn't sanitizing user input properly, which could lead to SQL injection attacks. This is a major security risk affecting the Search API and reported by customer CUST-0018. @eid_e01a396c, this one's for you.", "utterranceID": "20260822-1-9cfec"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260822-1-9cfec"}
