{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_99835861", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:55:00", "text": "Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current Salesforce issues. Let's take a look and see what we can learn! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261026-0-9fda9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-0-9fda9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_99835861", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:57:00", "text": "First up, there's a bug in OpenSSL related to weak encryption in data transmission. It seems similar to our Lead Data Export issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/625. @eid_9f4e2c6f, what do you think?", "utterranceID": "20261026-1-64dd1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-1-64dd1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9f4e2c6f", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:01:00", "text": "Thanks, Ian! This looks quite relevant. The outdated encryption algorithms in OpenSSL could give us insights into strengthening our encryption methods. I'll review the PR and see if there are any strategies we can apply. 🔒", "utterranceID": "20261026-2-ece17"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-2-ece17"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_99835861", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:04:00", "text": "Great, Ian! Next, there's a PR in the Electron project about UI freeze during heavy background processing. This is similar to our UI thread starvation issue. Check it out here: https://github.com/electron/electron/pull/626. Hannah, any thoughts?", "utterranceID": "20261026-3-6af1d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-3-6af1d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3f4b2681", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:06:00", "text": "This is spot on, Ian! The Electron issue with background tasks consuming too many resources is just like what we're seeing. I'll dive into their approach and see if we can optimize our resource management similarly. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261026-4-138be"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-4-138be"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_99835861", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:07:00", "text": "Awesome, Hannah! Lastly, there's a PostgreSQL bug about data corruption in concurrent writes. Sounds a lot like our Lead Database issue. Here's the PR: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/627. Can you take a look at this one too?", "utterranceID": "20261026-5-fa203"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-5-fa203"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_3f4b2681", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:12:00", "text": "Sure thing, Ian! The concurrent write operations causing data corruption in PostgreSQL could definitely give us some clues. I'll review their fix and see how we can apply it to our database operations. 🛠️", "utterranceID": "20261026-6-f6906"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-6-f6906"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-ianjones-LeadForce", "channelID": "ch-force-585771"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_99835861", "timestamp": "2026-10-26T09:16:00", "text": "Thanks, team! Let's use these insights to tackle our issues effectively. If you find anything particularly useful, let's discuss it further. Keep me posted on your progress! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261026-7-b4b11"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261026-7-b4b11"}
